'''Outsiders''' was a [[:category:Russia|Russian]] tag created by [[Virtus.pro]] in the wake of the [[wikipedia:Russian invasion of Ukraine|Russian invasion of Ukraine]]. Due to [[Virtus.pro]]'s ownership group having ties to companies and individuals sanctioned by American and European governments, the '''Outsiders''' tag was created as a neutral name for the roster.

==Timeline==
{{Tabs dynamic
|name1=2022
|name2=2023
|This=2
|content1=
*March 2nd - [[ESL]] announce that Russian organizations with ties to the government are indefinitely banned from competing in their events. <ref name="ban">{{cite web|url=https://www.hltv.org/news/33363/esl-pro-league-bans-organizations-with-ties-to-russian-government-from-upcoming-season|title=ESL Pro League bans "organizations with ties to the Russian government" from upcoming season|date=2022-03-02|author=[[Striker (Czech journalist)|Striker]]|publisher=[[HLTV]]}}</ref>
*March 4th - [[Virtus.pro]] confirm they will allow their team to play under a neutral name, which is later confirmed to be '''Outsiders'''. <ref name="outsiders">{{cite web|url=https://www.hltv.org/news/33371/virtuspro-criticize-esl-ban-allow-team-to-participate-in-epl-under-neutral-name|title=Virtus.pro criticize ESL ban; allow team to participate in EPL under neutral name|date=2022-03-04|author=[[Striker (Czech journalist)|Striker]]|publisher=[[HLTV]]}}</ref>
*April 9th - [[PGL]]  announce that they will be mirroring [[ESL]]'s decision to ban Russian organizations with ties to the government. <ref name="pgl bans">{{cite web|url=https://www.hltv.org/news/33561/gambit-and-virtuspro-organizations-banned-from-pgl-rmrs-and-major|title=Gambit and Virtus.pro organizations banned from PGL RMRs and Major|date=2022-04-09|author=[[Striker (Czech journalist)|Striker]]|publisher=[[HLTV]]}}</ref>
*May 23rd - [[Virtus.pro]] bench [[buster]] and [[YEKINDAR]]. <ref name="buster YEK benched">{{cite web|url=https://virtus.pro/en/articles/virtuspro-perevodit-buster-i-yekindar-v-zapas|title=Virtus.pro moves buster and YEKINDAR out of the active roster|date=2022-05-23|publisher=[[Virtus.pro]]}}</ref>
*May 31st - [[Virtus.pro]] acquire [[n0rb3r7]] and [[fame]] from [[K23]]. <ref name="+n0rb3r7 +fame">{{cite web|url=https://virtus.pro/en/articles/sostav-virtuspro-po-csgo-ukomplektovan-n0rb3r7-i-fame-novye-igroki-komandy|title=Virtus.pro CS:GO roster is complete: n0rb3r7 and fame are new team members|date=2022-05-31|publisher=[[Virtus.pro]]}}</ref>
*October 14th - [[YEKINDAR]] buys himself out of his contract and leaves [[Virtus.pro]]. <ref name="YEKINDAR leaves">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/yek1ndar/status/1580981529563787266|title=Update on my situation|date=2022-10-14|author=[[YEKINDAR]]}}</ref>
*November 13th - '''Outsiders''' win the [[Intel_Extreme_Masters/2022/Rio|IEM Major]] in Rio de Janeiro, defeating [[Heroic]] 2-0 in the grand final.

|content2=
*January 8th - [[Virtus.pro]] bench [[n0rb3r7]] and acquire [[KaiR0N-]] from [[Aurora Gaming]]. <ref name="+KaiR0N">{{cite web|url=https://virtus.pro/en/articles/kair0n-prisoedinyaetsya-k-sostavu-virtuspro-po-csgo|title=KaiR0N- joins Virtus.pro CS:GO roster|date=2023-01-08|publisher=[[Virtus.pro]]}}</ref>
* January 17th - [[buster]] is acquired by [[Cloud9]]. <ref name="-buster">{{cite web|url=https://virtus.pro/en/articles/transfer-buster-perexodit-v-cloud9|title=Transfer deal: buster moves to Cloud9|date=2023-01-17|publisher=[[Virtus.pro]]}}</ref>
* March 22nd - [[BLAST]] lift their sanction against [[Virtus.pro]], as a result, they are allowed to participate in [[BLAST]]-organized events under the tag going forward. <ref name="ban lift">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/virtuspro/status/1638520953519874050|title=Virtus.pro to be reintegrated into BLAST and ESL tournaments|date=2023-03-22|author=[[Virtus.pro]]}}</ref>
* March 28th - [[ESL]] lift their sanction against [[Virtus.pro]], as a result, they are allowed to participate in [[ESL]]-organized events under the tag going forward. As a result of these changes, the '''Outsiders''' tag is retired. <ref name="ban lift"/>
}}

